# SRG-APP-000027-AU-000590  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must automatically audit account modification.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000027-AU-000590
group:           V-221901
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001403
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    Splunk writes an audit event whenever a user or role object is modified,
                 generation of which is not configurable; the application's configurable
                 share is that those audit events are queued to an index, and that the
                 edit_user capability is held only by the roles the organization intends,
                 so each modification record is attributable to an authorized
                 administrator.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.

check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        Modifications made to an identity in an external LDAP directory or SAML
                 identity provider are audited by that component, not by Splunk; Splunk
                 records only the role mapping and account changes made on itself.
external:        Which roles are permitted to hold the edit_user capability declared in
                 authorize.conf [capability::edit_user] is an organizational access control
                 decision; the capability stanza's absence from a local configuration file
                 is not a defect, because the product ships the capability definition and
                 its default role assignments.
external:        Where audit queueing is false by design, an inputs.conf monitor stanza
                 tailing the audit log carries retention.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/audit.conf.spec:23-29 ([auditTrail] queueing =
                 <boolean>, default true); splunk-spec-files/authorize.conf.spec:719-728
                 ([capability::edit_user]: "Lets a user create, edit, or remove other
                 users"); SRG-APP-000027-AU-000590 check and fix text.
finding:         Audit records for account modification are generated by Splunk but not
                 retained in an index, because audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing is set to
                 false and no compensating monitor input is configured; this is assessed at
                 the application layer alone, and modifications performed in an external
                 directory service or identity provider are audited by that component,
                 which is recorded as an external dependency.
